Track 2: "Why Did You Miss the 4 PM Caravan?"
- Story & Context: Solder-burned apprentice Simran sat weeping beside a fractured Farfisa console at the Chani Oasis, scraping green copper patina from its tone generators with the tip of her rusted hairpin while the salt wind howled. She had stayed behind to re-wire the synthesizer's decaying ribbon cables while the evening trading convoy rolled away without her into the orange dust storm, stranding her alone with an unamplified tumbi and a leaking lithium battery cell. In the eerie stillness, she locked the machine into a three-note Phrygian synth chord, running it through a damaged reel-to-reel deck to answer the howling wind while camel bells drifted beyond the dunes. Her cracked lips parted against the dry gale, humming "You left the trade-gate open while the second-hand froze in my throat."
